steps.body:
In each ad (Destination → URL parameters) set:
utm_source=facebook&utm_medium=paid&utm_campaign={{campaign.id}}&utm_content={{ad.id}}&utm_term={{adset.id}}
Hullwise ties orders to the ad and the ad set through them; ads without them are flagged.

Account settings → Tracking → tracking template:
{lpurl}?utm_source=google&utm_medium=cpc&utm_campaign={campaignid}&utm_content={creative}&utm_term={keyword}
Hullwise ties orders to ads ({creative}) and keywords ({keyword}) through it; campaigns without it are flagged on the Suggestions page.

In every ad set the URL parameters (or append them to the landing page URL):
{utmTemplate}
TikTok fills __CAMPAIGN_ID__, __AID__ (ad group) and __CID__ (ad). Together with the ttclid click id they tie orders to campaigns, ad groups and ads; ads without them are flagged on the Suggestions page.

Spoki → Settings → Webhook (outbound and inbound messages) → paste:
{webhookUrl}
The last part of the URL is the store's secret: do not share it. Spoki sends the same message again for each new status (sent, delivered, read, error).

Give it a name (e.g. Hullwise) and paste:
{serverUrl}
Leave the advanced OAuth fields empty: Claude registers itself with Hullwise.
